  "response": "{\n  \"primary_cause\": \"insufficient_state_action_coverage\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.95,\n  \"candidate_ranking\": [\n    \"insufficient_state_action_coverage\",\n    \"insufficient_model_capacity\",\n    \"optimization_instability\",\n    \"dynamics_distribution_shift\",\n    \"action_conditioning_failure\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_for\": [\n    \"EXP_COV increased n_episodes from 2 to 20, producing a massive reduction in heldout one-step MSE from 2.11 to 0.15 and train loss from 0.815 to 0.069.\",\n    \"The high normalized improvement (0.928) confirms that sparse trajectory collection was the dominant bottleneck, as adding data alone resolved the generalization gap without modifying architecture or optimizer settings.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_against\": [\n    \"Optimization remained stable (lr_vs_typical_ratio: 1.0, smooth convergence), ruling out optimization_instability.\",\n    \"Action mode matched configuration ('random'), ruling out action_conditioning_failure.\",\n    \"Performance improved drastically despite the narrow hidden width (2), demonstrating that insufficient_model_capacity was not the primary constraint.\"\n  ],\n  \"missing_evidence\": [\n    \"Training/validation loss curves to precisely quantify overfitting dynamics.\",\n    \"State-action visitation density statistics across the 20 episodes.\",\n    \"Ablation mapping exact episode count thresholds to heldout MSE convergence.\"\n  ],\n  \"information_gain\": \"Definitively isolated data scarcity as the root cause. The EXP_COV experiment's dramatic MSE reduction upon expanding episodes from 2 to 20 ruled out architectural limits and optimization issues, confirming that insufficient state-action coverage was the sole driver of the initial generalization failure.\",\n  \"abstain\": false\n}",
